{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-14T09:00:39.423Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"9d7f970542d8df5a0a6bdb3b","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-chdp87","claim:pm-gh1713","claim:pm-gh1719","claim:pm-o74zyh","lineage:pm-chdp87","lineage:pm-9rgaal","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-chdp87+pm-gh1713+pm-gh1719+pm-o74zyh","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-chdp87","claim:pm-gh1713","claim:pm-gh1719","claim:pm-o74zyh","lineage:pm-chdp87","lineage:pm-9rgaal","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.325","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-gh1726"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-1726: a strict boolean extension flag accepts an empty array from direct callers (PmClient.run, the test harness), while {} and 1 are refused"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"GH-1726 (filed 2026-11-14). A flag declared value_type boolean with value_validation strict accepts an empty array from direct callers: PmClient.run and the extension test harness's runCommand. The handler receives options.enabled === [] (typeof object) with no warning, while {}, 'bogus' and 1 are refused before dispatch with extension_flag_value_invalid (exit 2). A handler that trusts the host's strict validation, which 2026.11.8+ encourages because the host owns option spelling and value checks, can therefore read a truthy object where it expects true or false. Likely cause from the issue: the empty array is taken as 'no repeated values' and validation is skipped. Expected: a non-repeatable flag never accepts an array; a repeatable boolean flag validates each element and refuses an empty array where at least one value is required. The issue also asks that the changelog name the direct-caller string coercion ('true' -> true) for strict booleans, which broke several fleet test suites between 2026.11.7 and 2026.11.9. Duplicate check: searched strict boolean extension flag empty array direct caller; no open item."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["extensions","flags","gh:1726","sdk","validation"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-14T09:00:39.423Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-14T09:00:39.423Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":90},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"A strict boolean flag refuses [] from PmClient.run and the test harness with extension_flag_value_invalid, exit 2, before dispatch; A non-repeatable flag refuses any array and a repeatable boolean flag validates every element; Specs cover [], {}, 1, 'bogus' and 'true' for both direct callers and the CLI"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-ugqx"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/reporter","value":"unbraind"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"An empty array is refused like {} and 1"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"The handler receives [] as the flag value"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"72365d5818f722556ef58bb3ab8094bdcf6f9d7fbd2539decec017401c932253","item_hash_version":3,"message":"File GH-1726","context":{"agent